@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

hpc:Serviceclass a owl:Class .
hpc:Guaranteepool a owl:Class .
hpc:Guarantee a owl:Class .
hpc:serviceclasscontainer a owl:ObjectProperty .
hpc:hasguarantee a owl:ObjectProperty .
hpc:name a owl:DatatypeProperty .
hpc:type a owl:DatatypeProperty .
hpc:distribution a owl:DatatypeProperty .
hpc:hosts a owl:DatatypeProperty .

rdfs:domain hpc:Serviceclasscontainer rdf:Property .
rdfs:domain hpc:Hasguarantee rdf:Property .
rdfs:range hpc:Serviceclass rdf:Property .
rdfs:range xsd:string rdf:Property .

hpc:ServiceClassContainer rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:type .
hpc:HasGuarantee rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:type .


This ontology fragment defines classes for `ServiceClass`, `GuaranteePool`, and `Guarantee`, as well as properties for `ServiceClassContainer`, `HasGuarantee`, `Name`, `Type`, `Distribution`, and `Hosts`. The properties have their domains and ranges defined. However, it does not include the host-based resources (slots, hosts, or packages) as the documentation does not provide ontology-worthy facts about them.
